text:
To dare, fear, love, and hate oneself; gladly to be tormented by glory; to forget to forget one's troubles; amid flame to burn without catching fire;


to see oneself lonely among people and accompanied by loneliness; continually to die yet never end; to lose oneself to find a means of loss;


to be a rich Fugger of luckless hopes, spend all one's wealth on suffering, and conquer hard stone with wax: us


these are Love's effects in my laments. Let no one call him god—that is madness—for his torments belong more to an executioner.
